 "why": "CLINC retained; MTOP added. MTOP has the strongest measured tier separation in the suite (+0.342 vs clinc +0.239) because its 102 intents cluster into 11 real domains, so near-band siblings are same-object/different-verb (create/delete/get/snooze alarm) -- the dense structure CLINC's flat multi-domain taxonomy lacks. Its far tier is also the cleanest in the suite (text-free picker 0.060, under the 0.125 gate). Caveat to report: MTOP is G3 for BOTH model families (intent is trained for deberta via MASSIVE/Banking77 and for Laya via support triage), so it adds no rung diversity; GoEmotions can be re-added if a G4*-for-Laya domain is wanted.",
